# Sitevento Widget Drafts

Standalone, self-contained HTML files (no external dependencies). Open any
one directly in a browser to preview it. Nothing here is wired into the
real app yet — once the set feels complete, these get ported into React
components under `app/w/[widgetId]/widgets/` and added to `WIDGET_CATALOG`
in `lib/widgets.ts`.

---

### email-capture.html
**Email Capture — full-screen popup**
A blurred-overlay email signup modal. Maps to the existing `email-capture`
catalog widget (scroll-end position).

### countdown-bar.html
**Countdown Timer — cartoonic announcement bar**
A sticky top bar with a live countdown and a close control. Maps to the
existing `countdown-timer` catalog widget (fixed-top position).

### support-chat.html
**Support Chat — lime AI chat bubble**
A floating chat launcher that expands into a chat panel. Maps to the
existing `support-chat` catalog widget (corner-bottom-right position).

### visitor-pulse.html
**Live Visitor Pulse — new widget**
A quiet, dismissible corner badge showing honest, already-tracked signals
("3 people viewing this page", "12 people viewed this today") with a soft
pulsing-dot animation. No fake urgency, no invented events — every line
is derived from view-tracking data Sitevento already collects via
`/api/track`. Deliberately does NOT claim live signups, since there's no
signup/conversion event in the schema today.

### spin-reward.html
**Daily Spin Reward — new widget**
A closeable "Spin & save" tab that opens a prize wheel. One real spin per
visitor per 24h (localStorage-gated). Odds are shown on-screen and the
wheel's stopping angle is computed from the already-chosen prize, so the
visual result always matches the outcome — no fake "so close!" near-miss
rigging.

### appointment-booking.html
**Appointment & Demo Booking — new widget**
Multi-step flow: choose a service → pick a date/time → enter details →
status. Built for agencies/consultants/SaaS "book a demo" use cases.
Key behavior: a slot is shown as **"Requested · not yet confirmed"**
immediately on submit, and only flips to **"Confirmed"** after a
simulated backend round-trip — this file never shows a slot as booked
before a backend would actually confirm it. Availability is "fetched"
per selected date with a loading state (simulated here), modeling where
a real calendar/freebusy integration would plug in. Comments in the
script note where lead-creation and conflict-handling would hook into
the real backend.

### campaign-bar.html
**Smart Announcement & Campaign Bar — new widget**
General-purpose announcement bar covering launches, promos, alerts, and
maintenance notices as swappable variants/themes (not four separate
widgets). Preview controls let you switch variant, position (top/bottom),
and page-targeting so you can see how a campaign scoped to e.g.
`/pricing` only would actually stay hidden everywhere else — the demo's
meta chip shows what's being targeted and whether the bar would be
showing on "this" page, rather than silently implying it runs everywhere.
Comments note where variant assignment, per-variant click/dismissal
beacons, and timezone-aware scheduling would hook into the real backend.

### feedback-survey.html
**Feedback & Satisfaction Survey — new widget**
Covers NPS (0–10 + reason), CSAT (star rating), and a short exit-intent
survey from one widget. Never shows unprompted — the demo's trigger
buttons stand in for the real trigger conditions (time-on-page, a custom
action event the site owner fires, exit-intent), each opt-in per campaign
with a frequency cap so the same visitor isn't asked repeatedly. "Not
now"/"Skip"/dismiss are tracked separately from an actual submitted
response so response-rate numbers in the dashboard aren't inflated by
people who just closed it. Comments note where segmentation (plan,
signup date, etc.) would come from the site owner's own identify call
rather than being guessed.

### contact-us.html
**Contact Us — new widget**
A real, direct contact form: name, email, message, submit. Not the
AI/chat-thread experience support-chat.html offers — this is the plain
"reach a human" form. Validates each field inline (red outline + inline
error, not a generic alert), shows a spinner while "sending," and only
plays the animated checkmark success state after a send would actually
succeed — a failed send shows an inline error banner and preserves what
was typed rather than pretending it worked. Comments note it would post
to this app's own API and write into the same Leads collection
email-capture already uses, so contact submissions show up in the
dashboard alongside everything else.

### reviews-carousel.html
**Reviews & Testimonials Carousel — new widget**
The one **manual-only**, inline-embedded widget in the set — unlike the
other nine it never auto-mounts into a corner/bar; the site owner places
it directly inside their own page content (e.g. a "What customers say"
section), matching the `manual-only` position case already named in
`lib/widgets.ts`. Auto-advancing carousel with arrows + dots, star
ratings, verified badges, and an aggregate rating line. Reviews shown
here are static sample content for the preview only — the real widget
never fabricates reviews or an aggregate score; both come from either
reviews the owner typed into the dashboard directly or a synced
connected review source, with the "last synced" line reflecting that
same real sync, never a cosmetic placeholder next to genuine-looking
content.

---

## Status
All 10 are draft/demo only — not yet ported into the Next.js app or wired
to real data (Firestore, calendar APIs, etc). Say when the set is ready
and we'll start converting them into real catalog widgets one at a time.
